# Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# The simulation runs in web workers over SharedArrayBuffer, which browsers
# only expose to cross-origin-isolated documents. Without these two headers
# `arrayBuffer()` silently falls back to a plain ArrayBuffer, the workers
# mutate copies, and the wall renders but never moves.
#
# `credentialless` lets the page load cross-origin images (the R2 bucket)
# without those objects carrying CORP. Safari does not support it, which is
# why functions/_middleware.js upgrades iOS to `require-corp` - for that path
# the R2 objects must be uploaded with
# `Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin` (see docs/deploy.md).
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: credentialless

# Hashed asset filenames change whenever content changes, so they can be
# cached indefinitely.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
